<title>CHINA: China Xinjiang grain output tops 8.0 mln T in '96.</title>
<headline>China Xinjiang grain output tops 8.0 mln T in '96.</headline>
<text>
<p>BEIJING, Jan 2 (Reuter) China's northwest region of Xinjiang produced more than 8.0 million tonnes of grain in 1996, an increase of 700,000 tonnes from the previous year's bumper crop, the Farmers' Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Land under grain totalled more than 1.6 million hectares (4.0 million acres) last year, an increase of 45,000 hectares (111,000 acres) from 1995 and surpassing planting targets, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
